    "body": "It looks like this was fixed/added to master at some point, maybe as part of the format strings work. I'm currently running a recent build of the master but it seems to work as you would expect\r\n```\r\n❯ starship explain\r\n\r\n Here's a breakdown of your prompt:\r\n ~/s/r/starship             -  The current working directory\r\n on  chore/update_clippy   -  The active branch of the repo in your current directory\r\n is 📦 v0.44.0        -  The package version of the current directory's project\r\n via 🦀 v1.45.0             -  The currently installed version of Rust\r\n ❯                          -  A character (usually an arrow) beside where the text is entered in your terminal\r\n```\r\n\r\nI'll pop this in the `v0.45.0` release as this should be included as part of that release.",
